WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:05.279
It's been, gosh, almost two whole decades
since Firefly went off the air, and the show's

00:00:05.279 --> 00:00:09.670
fans have been peppered with false hope at
least once a year ever since.

00:00:09.670 --> 00:00:14.630
Rumors of reunion specials, Serenity sequels,
and Netflix reboots have made the rounds like

00:00:14.630 --> 00:00:16.770
so many signals you can't stop.

00:00:16.770 --> 00:00:21.730
Nathan Fillion cosplayed as Captain Reynolds
on Castle, which devotees saw as a sure sign

00:00:21.730 --> 00:00:23.919
that the crew would keep flying soon enough.

00:00:23.919 --> 00:00:29.050
An MMO was announced in 2013, complete with
voice work from the original cast, but it

00:00:29.050 --> 00:00:33.450
disappeared without so much as a "sorry we
got you all worked up" from the development

00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:34.450
team.

00:00:34.450 --> 00:00:38.230
It is, therefore, with some degree of caution
that the following update is relayed: Word

00:00:38.230 --> 00:00:42.730
is making the rounds that Disney is working
on a Firefly reboot, intended for release

00:00:42.730 --> 00:00:44.890
on its Disney+ streaming service.

00:00:44.890 --> 00:00:50.220
That update comes courtesy of Giant Freakin
Robot, and while a reminder to do like The

00:00:50.220 --> 00:00:54.660
Who taught you and not get fooled again might
come as a given, the rumor appears to have

00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:55.660
legs.

00:00:55.660 --> 00:01:00.220
It's all thanks to the continuing downturn
in the financial viability of theatrical releases,

00:01:00.220 --> 00:01:04.030
and a company-wide shift towards more televised
content.

00:01:04.030 --> 00:01:08.840
Firefly, which joined the Disney vault as
part of the company's 2019 acquisition of

00:01:08.840 --> 00:01:14.009
all Fox entertainment properties, is seen
as a viable universe to explore given the

00:01:14.009 --> 00:01:16.509
studio's direct-to-consumer emphasis.

00:01:16.509 --> 00:01:20.729
But it's not the return of a beloved cult
franchise that's turning the most heads — it's

00:01:20.729 --> 00:01:24.790
the rumored Disneyfication of the series that
appears to be coming with it.

00:01:24.790 --> 00:01:29.520
Per Giant Freakin Robot's source, Disney's
return to the Firefly universe is set to make

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:33.549
some staggering changes, not the least of
which is that the series would reportedly

00:01:33.549 --> 00:01:38.570
be a hard reboot, recasting and restarting
every character from the beginning.

00:01:38.570 --> 00:01:43.259
That's bound to draw the ire of diehard fans,
as will the studio's proposed plan to make

00:01:43.259 --> 00:01:48.150
the new series "PG rated" in the hopes of
creating a more family-friendly end product.

00:01:48.150 --> 00:01:54.350
Firefly, in its short-lived run on Fox back
in 2002, was a decidedly bleak story defined

00:01:54.350 --> 00:01:56.700
by its morally gray plots and characters.

00:01:56.700 --> 00:02:02.789
In the Firefly Universe, prostitution is a
noble line of work, dogs are eaten, and high-ranking

00:02:02.789 --> 00:02:06.529
boss battle minions get kicked into turbines
to better make a point.

00:02:06.529 --> 00:02:11.530
The good guys do bad things, and the bad guys
do worse things, with frequent allusions to

00:02:11.530 --> 00:02:17.290
forced brain surgery, wholesale civilian slaughter,
and sexual violence factoring into the show's

00:02:17.290 --> 00:02:18.290
plot.

00:02:18.290 --> 00:02:22.790
It seems like a peculiar universe to try and
sand the edges off of, but that's reportedly

00:02:22.790 --> 00:02:24.820
what Disney intends to do.

00:02:24.820 --> 00:02:29.200
Details on the show's production are slim
at the moment, with reports that the Firefly

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:34.159
reboot is in such early days that it wasn't
yet ready for Disney's recent Investors Day

00:02:34.159 --> 00:02:35.500
presentation.

00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:39.709
Perhaps the biggest question on fans' minds
will be whether or not original showrunner

00:02:39.709 --> 00:02:45.290
and series creator Joss Whedon will be involved,
given the recent string of bizarre allegations

00:02:45.290 --> 00:02:47.760
surrounding the acclaimed filmmaker.

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:52.299
There's no word yet, but it seems unlikely
that the show will break atmo without Whedon

00:02:52.299 --> 00:02:54.239
at least offering his two cents.

00:02:54.239 --> 00:02:58.390
While Browncoats wait for more news about
the rumored reboot, there's still plenty of

00:02:58.390 --> 00:03:00.270
Firefly lore to explore.

00:03:00.270 --> 00:03:03.260
Since the show went off the air, Dark Horse
and Boom!

00:03:03.260 --> 00:03:08.120
Studios have produced dozens of comic book
continuations of the story, written by geek

00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:12.189
royalty like Patton Oswalt and even Joss Whedon
himself.

00:03:12.189 --> 00:03:18.049
The franchise has spawned novelization, reference
books, RPGs, board games, and a cook book

00:03:18.049 --> 00:03:21.209
since its untimely removal from the airwaves.

00:03:21.209 --> 00:03:25.310
Given that the original series only lasted
half a season, the fact that it spawned so

00:03:25.310 --> 00:03:30.629
much content might seem impossible — but
then again, that's what makes it mighty.

